+### Usage statistics projection (2026-10-28)
+
+`GET /api/stats` applies its UTC half-open time window, profile/unprofiled scope and recorded dimension predicates to every aggregate, including workflow output. Invalid, duplicate or non-string recorded dimension values retain the operation-history resolver semantics. `sessionCount` counts distinct journal sessions containing matching operations (not conversations). The unfiltered scope request still supplies dimension filter options. `profileOperations` retains its time-window-only profile-chooser metadata contract and is not a selected-cohort KPI.
+
+SQL groups add nullable `logicalReadsMedianSum`, operation coverage (`logicalReadsAvailableOperations`, `logicalReadsUnavailableOperations`) and metric coverage (`logicalReadsAvailableMetrics`, `logicalReadsUnavailableMetrics`). The value sums available stored `operation_metrics.logical_reads_median` rows once per metric, across cases/variants. It does not multiply by measured repetitions and is not actual execution-total IO. Null means no recorded median; zero is recorded zero; any missing operations or metric rows make coverage partial. Operations with no metrics are counted as unavailable operations, not fabricated metric rows. Metrics are collapsed by operation before joining, preserving operation counts/durations. `topSqlByLogicalReads` ranks all matching SQL groups before the bounded top-20 projection; count/time orders retain their own full-population rankings.
+
+Usage presents a joined KPI band and the SQL logical-read order. Failed/rejected percentage is `(failed + rejected) / all matching operations`, unavailable for an empty cohort. Measured output includes only `accountingKind=workflow-output` bytes and their retained per-call byte-based token estimates; legacy artifact volumes, input/discovery/chat tokens and model prices are not substituted. The detailed accounting/chart disclosure is removed from the page; journal and API accounting contracts remain available.
